[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="TrialDef" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://modules/trials/trial_def.gd" id="1_task"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://modules/trials/trial_axis.gd" id="2_axis"]

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Axis_clutter"]
script = ExtResource("2_axis")
name = &"clutter"
easy = 3.0
hard = 8.0
driven = false
fixed = 6.0

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Axis_overlap"]
script = ExtResource("2_axis")
name = &"overlap"
easy = 0.0
hard = 1.0
driven = true

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Axis_contrast"]
script = ExtResource("2_axis")
name = &"contrast"
easy = 0.9
hard = 0.2
driven = false
fixed = 0.65

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_task")
title = "Find the object"
visual_skill = &"search"
axes = Array[ExtResource("2_axis")]([SubResource("Axis_clutter"), SubResource("Axis_overlap"), SubResource("Axis_contrast")])
notes = "Objects in clutter (design doc section 3).

Driven axis: overlap, and only overlap. Ostrovsky 2009 [2] found newly sighted
people could not separate still, overlapping objects, which makes occlusion the
variable worth adapting. Clutter count and contrast stay pinned so a failed round
is attributable to one thing; raise their fixed values by hand (or pin them from
the debug menu) to test a different point in the space.

contrast is Weber contrast against the surface the objects sit on:
c = (L_background - L_target) / L_background, target darker, measured on the
linear luminance of the albedo. Contrast.background_luminance must match the
table material (0.34 for shared/materials/floor.tres). Set it per surface.

clutter is capped by the number of distinct object scenes in the SearchTrial,
since each is placed at most once (naming one object needs exactly one of it).
Add scenes to widen the range.

Motion is not an axis here on purpose: it is hint level 2. Driving it from both
the staircase and the help system would move one variable from two places."
up_after = 2
step = 0.1
hint_after = 8.0
hint_fade = 1.5
max_hint = 3
probe_rounds = 3
probe_difficulty = 0.3
